Z||000021||ChopTop||08-29-2001||10:32 AM||||About 10 years ago on a very busy street this guy pulls right out in front of me, actually he pulled out right in front of everyone, he just happened to pull in too my lane when he did it.  I'm driving a 1975 cancer ridden yellow Chevy Monza.  The hood would start boucing up and down over 25 miles an hour, passenger door would fly open if you went to fast around a corner, half laudau roof, that of course flaps in the breeze, had to open the drivers window and lift it up in order for it to shut, you know, a real piece of $hit.   Anyway I could have done one of two things, slammed on my brakes and missed him, or...casually slam on the brakes.  I choose the latter and neatly kissed the back of his bumper, hard enough for him to know he'd been hit.  He slows down, I slow down, he pulls over into the right lane, I pull over into the right lane, he pulls into a parking lot expecting me to follow her, I slowed down just enough to let him see me wave as I went on my way.  Gosh, I miss that piece of $hit.||||reg||1
Z||000022||DreXteR||08-29-2001||10:37 AM||||firstfiero - Dont feel bad. Like rdmcneil said fat women need love too, hehehehe rofl.  She dont pass a month in here, ppl here drive like mad mans, but no one make anithing to you. Like any big city, too much ppl in 1 place.<P>87GTBro - Rofl thats exactly I have in mind  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Mach10 - Thats the attitiude!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Ppl in here are more relaxend in that situation, I believe is normal here to jump into a lane that fits only 1 ft more than ur car length.<P>Peace<P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000023||Ken Wittlief||08-29-2001||10:58 AM||||Its times like that when I wish I had saved the big cardboard tube from my carpet, cut off about a 6' section, painted it flat green, put a handle and sights on it, and stuffed a red nose cone in one end.<P> then when someone pulls up next to you and starts giving you kwrap you open the passenger window, open the drivers side window, and casually lift your 'Bazooka' up off the floor and start flipping the sights up.<P> you wont even have to point it at them -theyll be long gone before it gets to that.||||reg||10
Z||000024||Cheever3000||08-29-2001||11:07 AM||||Once I could tell some guys in a pickup were mad at me (probably my fault, I was young & stupid).  Caught in traffic at the next light, I got prepared in case they got out, and reached to the glove box for my nunchakus and sat them on my lap.  I think they believed I was getting a gun, because they suddenly left me alone.  That was back when most Americans had never seen numbchucks.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000025||Standard||08-29-2001||11:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>Its times like that when I wish I had saved the big cardboard tube from my carpet, cut off about a 6' section, painted it flat green, put a handle and sights on it, and stuffed a red nose cone in one end.<P> then when someone pulls up next to you and starts giving you kwrap you open the passenger window, open the drivers side window, and casually lift your 'Bazooka' up off the floor and start flipping the sights up.<P> you wont even have to point it at them -theyll be long gone before it gets to that.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>muhahahahahaha  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I like that idea!<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000026||MinnGreenGT||08-29-2001||11:26 AM||||Ok, so my friends and I may be a little strange, but we collect swords.  <P>A couple of my friends were cruising around (in a '95 Eclipse GSX, big wing, but not rice). When a couple of punks in a Riced-Out Honda started tailgating them.  The Honda guys were just freaking out already... not sure why, just generally pissed at the world.  They finally pulled up to a light, and both driver & passenger grabbed a conviently located sword.  The simply popped the doors open and stepped out, weapons in hand- looked like something from a Highlander film!  The Honda punks just sat there with a freaked-out-scared-need-some-new-underwear look on their faces.  My friends hopped back into the GSX and drove off as the light turned green.  The Honda boys disappeared at the first available turn.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000027||Formula88||08-29-2001||11:47 AM||||Fiero owners with swords...hmmm, where have I heard that before.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I had one chick tailgating me something crazy, I guess for pulling out in front of her, but I made sure she didn't have to slow down.  Anyway, since when people are following you, they tend to take the exact same line in traffic as you do, as I'm turning onto a side street, I purposely get as close to the curb as I possibly can.  Sure enough, she follows suit, but since she's looking at me and not the road - BUMP - right over the curb!  That was fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Then she follows me into the Taco Bell I was going to and gets outta the car with a baseball bat talking how she's gonna beat my a$$, etc., etc.  So I calmly get out of the car, walk behind her car (she's still yelling) as I dial 911 and phone in her plate.  She then got in her car and left and I filed the assult charges with the cop.  Nothing came of it though.  He went by her house and I think that scared her pretty good.  These days, I don't carry weapons in the car, but I'm thinking about changing that policy.  People are just getting too stupid, too easy.  <P>I would have loved to have seen the look on her face if I'd had MY sword with me when she pulled out our bat.  Probably would have scared her sh!tless.  <P>Concealed carry pistol permits are legal in NC.  I think I'm gonna be getting one.||||reg||6
Z||000028||TSPalmer||08-29-2001||11:52 AM||||You've just got to watch out now days.  If you jump out, they might just shoot you without any provocation.  Scary times....<P>------------------<BR>T.Shawn Palmer<BR>'85 SE 4cyl 5spd||||reg||11
Z||000029||starfighter007@msn.com||08-29-2001||12:07 PM||||who does that fat a$$ think she is If what your saying is true It was an accident I try to get along with evey body but this female dog I think would have pushed me over the edge  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000030||Ryan Wright||08-29-2001||01:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I know immediately what I would do, be on the phone calling the cops.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No kidding. "911 state your emergency." ... "Yeah, someone is following me around town and she keeps screaming that she's going to kill me, I think she might have a gun, I need an officer here now."<P>Problem solved. The cops will be there faster than you could imagine.<P>I already posted my incident of road rage earlier this month, but here's the short version for those who haven't seen it: I pulled out of my subdivision on my way to work. Didn't see a white VW Rabbit and pulled out in front of him. Oops. He got pissed, crossed the center line (two lanes on the road, one in each direction), passed me, then slammed on his brakes and jerked his car into my lane trying to get me to rear end him. I slammed on my brakes (wish I hadn't, he would have clipped my front bumper), jerked my steering wheel to avoid him, left 49 feet of rubber on the road and wrapped my '85 GT around a city light pole.<P>The SOB drove away. Just flat out left. He came back after the cops had arrived but since I didn't hit his vehicle, they just let him go. They said he was a witness to a one car accident. F****** bastards. Must have been a hot donut waiting back at the station. Anyway, I have another Fiero now, and my insurance company is suing the guy for causing an accident. I'm told if they win he will have to pay for everything out of his pocket, as his insurance will not cover it. I'm also told that when an insurance company sues you, you're pretty well f***ed. I hope they take his ass to the cleaners. Gonna be great when he has to come up with the money to pay for my car, the city light pole, my ER visit to have my knee x-rayed (it was just bruised), plus attorneys fees for both him and my insurance company. I can't wait to take the stand and testify with his sorry ass sitting there. Also can't wait for him to try to tell his poor ass story - that I became angry and tried to pass HIM (after he passed me) and that's when I hit the pole. The cops bought it, but nobody else will. Who leaves 49 feet of rubber in their own lane trying to pass somebody?<P>Pictures of my totalled car @ <A HREF="http://www.ryanwright.com/fiero/85gt/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ryanwright.com/fiero/85gt/</A> <P>------------------<BR>-Ryan Wright (http://www.ryanwright.com)||||reg||1
Z||000031||MinnGreenGT||08-29-2001||01:52 PM||||Ryan... just lookin' through your site. OUCH! that was a nasty one!  I hope you sue him for every penny.  BTW: also noticed that you bought TerryK's 3800s/c!! Congrats! I was trying to convince my wife to let me get that one- but to no avail.  Are you going to part out the '85GT? Email if you are able to sell parts!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
